    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nI want to use indentscope inside only my neovim file buffer but it shows those arrows animation in terminal buffer as well.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\njust do `:terminal` or any terminal plugins like [`nvterm`](https://github.com/nvchad/nvterm). Toggle with mouse ..\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI don't want those animations in my terminal buffer\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThis -> \r\n\r\n[poc.webm](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/90331517/98bb5ef5-df9e-4d67-bb3d-a7763f1e3993)\r\n",
